---
import SiteLayout from '../../components/SiteLayout.astro';
import { findPost } from '../../data/blog';

const post = findPost('the-part-ive-never-told')!;
---

<SiteLayout
  title={`${post.title} — Songdance`}
  description={post.excerpt}
  image={post.hero}
  imageAlt={post.heroAlt}
>
  <article class="bp">
    <header class="bp-head">
      <p class="sd-eyebrow">Journal · The story behind the journey · Part three</p>
      <h1 class="bp-title">The part I've never <em class="lyric">told</em>.</h1>
      <p class="bp-lede">
        Where the story turns — Upala's longing for something freer, the loss, and the course that
        grew from meeting grief in the body.
      </p>
      <p class="bp-byline">
        <time datetime={post.date}>{post.dateLabel}</time>
        <span class="bp-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {post.readingMinutes} min read
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="bp-hero">
      <img src={post.hero} alt={post.heroAlt} fetchpriority="high" />
    </figure>

    <div class="bp-body">
      <p>
        This is the third part of a longer story. It began with how the
        <a href="/blog/before-there-was-upala">Authentic Singing Journey started</a>, and went on to
        <a href="/blog/the-story-wasnt-over">what came after</a> — the journeys we made, and the way
        Upala moved. If you're just joining, those are the places to begin.
      </p>
      <p>
        After the Inner Child and Magical Movement journeys, something had quietly grown around us: a
        real worldwide community. That's when we began the <strong>Songdance Circle</strong> — we
        returned to our old weekly rhythm and promised everyone a brand-new session every single week.
      </p>
      <p>
        And we kept that promise. Thirty-minute dance flows, spoken stories set to music, meditations,
        visualisations, mantras — a whole stretch of wild, unhurried creation, most of it made while we
        were living in South Africa. We were even about to buy a house there. Everything was going well.
      </p>
      <p>
        …Until — and this is the part I've never really told — something in Upala began to long for
        something else. Something even freer than anything we were making.
      </p>
      <p>
        It was as if she wanted to dance and sound among the stars — a kind of freedom I'm not sure is
        possible here, on this earthly plane. Not that she wanted to die. Not at all. In her final
        months she began recording an album, and she still wanted to record a free dance ritual. But
        alongside that longing, something in her was simply tired.
      </p>
      <p>
        So we stopped travelling and settled back in Belgium. Shortly after, the tumour returned — and
        an intense stretch of rapid decline followed.
      </p>

      <p class="bp-turn">And then she moved on.</p>

      <p>
        What came after was, for me, a full stop. For a long while I wanted to stop Songdance altogether
        and do something — anything — else. It was often simply too painful.
      </p>

      <figure class="bp-figure">
        <img
          src="/media/library/forgiveness-daniela-and-jacob.webp"
          alt="Daniela Hess and Jacob together, smiling"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Daniela and me. The Grief Course grew from her decades with grief, and mine with sound.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        But two dear friends, Daniela and Christopher, stayed close. Gently, patiently, they helped me
        turn something almost unbearable into something that could carry me back toward my purpose — and
        toward my own life-energy again. That's where <strong>The Grief Course</strong> was born: out of
        Daniela's decades of counselling grief, and my own experience of meeting grief in the body,
        through sound.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="bp-pull">
        <p>Grief is not the pain. It is the process that helps you move through it.</p>
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        It's for anyone living through a big, irrevocable change — because where there is change, there
        is grief. Not to rush it, or to "heal" it away, but to be with it, and to let it move.
      </p>

      <p class="bp-signoff">Her sound is still here.<br />With love,<br />Jacob</p>
    </div>

    <aside class="bp-cta">
      <p class="sd-eyebrow">The course it became</p>
      <h2 class="bp-cta-head">You don't have to cross <em class="lyric">alone.</em></h2>
      <p class="bp-cta-body">
        Four sessions with Daniela and me, to meet your grief — of any size — in a conscious, gentle
        way. Lifetime access, and you can begin whenever you're ready.
      </p>
      <a href="/courses/grief" class="bp-cta-btn">
        Discover The Grief Course
        <i class="ph-light ph-arrow-right"></i>
      </a>
    </aside>

    <nav class="bp-back">
      <a href="/blog"><i class="ph-light ph-arrow-left"></i> All journal entries</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .bp {
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* ---------- Header ---------- */
  .bp-head {
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--sp-9) var(--sp-6) var(--sp-6);
  }
  .bp-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5.2vw, 60px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-display);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: var(--sp-4) 0 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  /* Typography law: Cormorant italic reads small inside Spectral display — bump it. */
  .bp-title em.lyric {
    font-family: var(--font-lyric);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.05em;
    color: var(--ember);
  }
  .bp-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-lyric);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(21px, 2.6vw, 28px);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 36ch;
    margin: var(--sp-5) 0 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .bp-byline {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-caption);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--ink-quiet);
    margin: var(--sp-5) 0 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
  }
  .bp-byline .bp-dot {
    width: 3px;
    height: 3px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink-whisper);
  }

  /* ---------- Hero image ---------- */
  .bp-hero {
    max-width: var(--container);
    margin: var(--sp-6) auto 0;
    padding: 0 var(--sp-6);
  }
  .bp-hero img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    filter: var(--sd-img-filter);
  }

  /* ---------- Body ---------- */
  .bp-body {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--sp-7) var(--sp-6) 0;
  }
  .bp-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-body-lg);
    line-height: var(--lh-prose);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--sp-5);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  /* Plain emphasis stays in the body italic (no lyric swap → no bump needed). */
  .bp-body em {
    font-style: italic;
  }
  /* A deliberate lyric flourish — swaps to Cormorant, so it must be sized up. */
  .bp-body em.lyric {
    font-family: var(--font-lyric);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.25em;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--ember-deep);
  }
  /* In-prose links — an ember underline that reads as part of the sentence. */
  .bp-body a {
    color: var(--ember-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    transition: color var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .bp-body a:hover {
    color: var(--plum);
  }

  /* The pivot line — set apart, in the lyric hand, quiet and heavy. */
  .bp-body p.bp-turn {
    font-family: var(--font-lyric);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 27px);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: var(--sp-6) 0 var(--sp-6);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .bp-figure {
    margin: var(--sp-7) 0;
  }
  .bp-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    filter: var(--sd-img-filter);
  }
  .bp-figure figcaption {
    margin: var(--sp-3) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-lyric);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink-quiet);
    text-align: center;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .bp-pull {
    margin: var(--sp-7) 0;
    padding: var(--sp-1) 0 var(--sp-1) var(--sp-5);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--ember);
  }
  .bp-pull p {
    font-family: var(--font-lyric);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(23px, 2.8vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .bp-body p.bp-signoff {
    font-family: var(--font-lyric);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-top: var(--sp-7);
  }

  /* ---------- Closing CTA ---------- */
  .bp-cta {
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: var(--sp-8) auto 0;
    padding: var(--sp-7) var(--sp-6);
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
  }
  .bp-cta-head {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--t-h2);
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: var(--sp-3) 0 0;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .bp-cta-head em.lyric {
    font-family: var(--font-lyric);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.05em;
    color: var(--ember-deep);
  }
  .bp-cta-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-prose);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: var(--sp-4) 0 0;
    max-width: 48ch;
  }
  .bp-cta-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: var(--sp-6);
    background: var(--ember-deep);
    color: var(--paper);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 14px 28px;
    border-radius: var(--r-pill);
    transition: background var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .bp-cta-btn:hover {
    background: var(--plum);
  }
  .bp-cta-btn i {
    font-size: 17px;
    transition: transform var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .bp-cta-btn:hover i {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  /* ---------- Back link ---------- */
  .bp-back {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: var(--sp-7) auto var(--sp-9);
    padding: 0 var(--sp-6);
  }
  .bp-back a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .bp-back a:hover {
    color: var(--ember-deep);
  }
  .bp-back i {
    font-size: 16px;
    transition: transform var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .bp-back a:hover i {
    transform: translateX(-4px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .bp-head {
      padding: var(--sp-8) var(--sp-5) var(--sp-5);
    }
    .bp-hero {
      padding: 0 var(--sp-5);
    }
    .bp-body {
      padding: var(--sp-6) var(--sp-5) 0;
    }
    .bp-cta {
      padding: var(--sp-6) var(--sp-5);
      margin-left: var(--sp-5);
      margin-right: var(--sp-5);
    }
    .bp-back {
      padding: 0 var(--sp-5);
    }
  }
</style>
